title: Subject to the Higher Powers: Romans 13 and the Christian
description: Posts from the channel on Romans 13: being subject to the powers ordained of God, rendering to Caesar and to God, Paul's example in chains, and why there is no political solution to a spiritual problem.
output: lessons/posts/pulled-romans-13-higher-powers.html

# From the posts of 2022-08-03 (two), 2022-11-09, 2023-03-07 and 2023-06-30 (three)
# (studies/data/notes/pulled-romans-13-higher-powers.html), in the author's words, with the review's cuts and fixes.

=== Introduction
--- Subject to the Higher Powers [title]
overline: From the channel
heading: Subject to the Higher Powers
sub: Romans 13 and the Christian. It is saved believers turning towards God that saves a nation.
refs: Romans 13:1-7; Mark 12:17; 2 Chronicles 7:14
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the slides. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

=== The higher powers
--- Let every soul be subject
kicker: Romans 13
scripture: Romans 13:1 | mark: the powers that be are ordained of God
p: God puts the people in power over us, to His purpose. Even the wicked.

--- Whosoever resisteth the power
scripture: Romans 13:2
p: Damnation in this sense for the saved is physical, but in the broader sense it is a sin to revolt against things that aren't contradicted by the higher power, the highest being God.

--- Think of Daniel
scripture: Romans 13:3 | mark: do that which is good, and thou shalt have praise of the same
p: Think of Daniel, given us for an example. He never compromised what was right, but did well in that framework that even under evil powers, he prospered.
refs: Daniel 1:8; Daniel 6:3-5

--- The minister of God
scripture: Romans 13:4-5 | mark: he beareth not the sword in vain

--- Liberty itself as a god
lead: ACAB. FAAFO. Molon labe. Don't tread on me.
p: The twisting of our liberty in Christ and the blessings that follow, into a cult of individuality that worships Liberty itself as a god leads to entitlement, pride, justification for wickedness and an abandonment of fear of God, and an adoption of fear of EVERYTHING that may infringe on our "freedoms."

--- The meek shall inherit the earth
lead: But we know, the meek shall inherit the earth. We know that we, as peacemakers are blessed. That as much as possible if it be within us, we should live peaceably with all men.
refs: Matthew 5:5; Matthew 5:9; Romans 12:18

--- Liberty comes from faith
p: Jews, who are in open rebellion against God, who killed the prophets and Christ Jesus, are contrary to all men and God's wrath abides upon them to the uttermost.
refs: 1 Thessalonians 2:15-16
callout: The shift from understanding that liberty comes from faith through Christ by grace, to it being something we deserve in itself, is a Jewish trick.

--- Tocqueville
p: Tocqueville, the Frenchman who toured early America concluded that the preservation of America’s traditional religion, the Puritan and Baptist faith in Christ, and the understanding that our liberty is from sin, through Him, is one of the most important tasks of democratic statesmanship.
p: He wrote that religion “should be considered the first” of America’s “political institutions” and even that it is necessary for Americans to “maintain Christianity…at all cost.”

=== Render to Caesar
--- Tempting Jesus
kicker: Mark 12
p: The Pharisees who have decided they need to kill Jesus come tempting Him to say something rebellious against Roman occupation. They flatter Jesus and then ask if the Jews should pay taxes to the empire.
p: Jesus, in a verse even the godless heathens know, shows that Caesar is on the coin of the realm, and declares;
big: Mark 12:17 | mark: Render to Caesar the things that are Caesar’s, and to God the things that are God’s

--- Render to God what is His
p: The amount of discomfort and twisting of this doctrine by those whose love of money, the material, has kept them from rendering to God what is His for generations, in every Christian culture.
p: There is always the religious equivalent of Sovereign Citizens who balk at the idea of giving "their money" to the beast system. Here Jesus says it's not yours. It's not God's. It's the beast's and the beast exacts tribute.
callout: The point isn't even to pay your taxes, though you shouldn't care if you have to, but to RENDER TO GOD what is His.

--- God judges nations
lead: If we as a nation, a people, willingly did that, the tax thing would take care of itself, because we get the government we deserve as a people. God judges nations.
p: The nation of Judea was 40yrs from its final destiny. God vowed to destroy it, and Jesus' prophecy came true and Judea was destroyed, just like the unfaithful servants at the vineyard.
refs: Mark 12:9; Luke 19:43-44

--- This is how a people die
p: And it was in a fit of rebellion that the last of the Jews were crushed, following a false messianic figure in the **Bar Kokhba revolt,** 70 years after that.
p: What never occurred to these seditious and adulterous Jews was repentance to God and acceptance of Jesus as Christ.
p: They followed man and wrath and fear instead. They made it their idol. They worshipped themselves and despised God's longsuffering mercy on them.
take: This is how a people die. This is how a nation is judged.

--- Tribute to whom tribute is due
scripture: Romans 13:6-7 | mark: Render therefore to all their dues
p: We are instructed by the Bible to not riot in the daytime or take vengeance for ourselves. To render custom to who is due custom and tribute to who is due tribute.
p: To render unto Caesar that which is Caesar's. To pay our taxes and obey the laws so long as they do not contradict the authority of the Lord and His word.

--- Every one in his place
p: Pastors to subject themselves to Jesus, servants to their masters, husbands to loving their wives as Christ loves His brethren, wives to be subject to their husbands and children to honor their parents.
refs: Romans 13:13; Romans 12:19; Ephesians 5:22-25; Ephesians 6:1-5

=== Paul in chains
--- The irony
lead: I was just struck with a realization about the irony of those who call Christianity "cucked," and who attempt to discredit the writings of the Apostle Paul based on his Epistles regarding the behavior of Christians, especially relative to the powers that be.
p: To the government. Being subject to those who have power over us, given by God. To, as much as possible, live at peace with all men. Romans 13, etc.

--- Bound for the gospel
p: The irony being that Paul was subject to constant persecution, was stoned to death at one point, had to be snuck out of cities in baskets lest the mobs led by Jews tear him apart, and who wrote a majority of his epistles from chains. Literally bound for preaching the word of God and the gospel of Christ crucified.
refs: Acts 14:19; Acts 9:23-25; 2 Corinthians 11:32-33; Ephesians 6:20

--- The only way we win
p: To have faith that God will save us from tribulation and persecution. To allow God to exact vengeance for us. To glory in our persecution for His name's sake.
callout: This isn't being "cucked," it's literally the only way we win.
p: And Paul, who wrote much of this from a jail cell, under house arrest, bound to a centurion by chains 24 hours a day for the cause of Christ, saw no contradiction in any of that.
refs: Acts 28:16; Acts 28:20

--- Glory in your affliction
p: As long as you're preaching the word of God, you shouldn't worry about things like hate crime laws or censorship, or any other persecution led by the Jews. Glory in your affliction and speak the truth.
p: In Acts, Peter, James, Paul and others are openly condemned and set upon for vocally pointing out that the Jews were antichrists who killed Christ Jesus. Stephen was martyred for "hate speech" against the Jews.
refs: Acts 5:40-42; Acts 7:51-60; Romans 5:3

--- A line in the sand
lead: These meek and humble servants, who turned the world upside down with their preaching, drew a line in the sand.
p: They turned the other cheek, loved their enemies, heaping coals upon the heads of those who hated them by their charity and humble conversation. Living peaceably.
p: But when it came to the preaching of the word and the truth of those who hate Christ, they boldly spoke out, despite threats of jail, and even unto death.
refs: Acts 17:6; Romans 12:20; Acts 4:29
take: Would that we are blessed by God with so strong a faith.

=== Without fear
--- Despising government
p: I find people not amenable to the literal reading of Romans 13:1-7 are despising government because they are harboring sinful, wrathful thoughts and don't want to believe that puts them directly on the path of
big: Romans 13:4 | mark: if thou do that which is evil, be afraid; for he beareth not the sword in vain
p: Or maybe they know, and want to escape the sword. Or maybe they are afraid of the implied persecution. Maybe they fear it becoming actual.

--- We must answer to the higher power
p: The point is when it comes to those matters that may turn hypothetical into reality, like supporting biblical doctrine on sodomites and adulterers, for example, or understanding that Jews are antichrists, by definition, bodily autonomy as a temple of the Holy Spirit, etc, in faith, without fear, and accepting that you may be persecuted for His sake, we must answer to the higher power, which is God.
refs: Acts 5:29; 1 John 2:22; 1 Corinthians 6:19

--- Make them say it
lead: Until then, we live of no offense. Paying tribute. Paying custom. Not breaking the law, until the law is explicitly anti-Christ.
center: Make them say it.
center: Make them say your salvation is hate and they want to shut it down.

=== No political solution
--- I love my people
lead: I love my people. I want to secure a future for my people's children.
p: And so I win souls. I raise Godly children. I live as blameless as I can. I suffer the little indignities and seek to have patience and understanding that God's judgment of our nation is just, and that the only way to reverse or delay His wrath is to turn from our evil ways that He may repent of the evil He would do.
refs: Jeremiah 18:7-8

--- We cannot vote our way out
lead: We cannot vote our way out. There is no political solution to a spiritual problem.
p: There is no rushing to violence either. Feds and glowies, keeping our people in fear and constantly reacting, seek to push us to violence, and in the violence justify the sword used against us.

--- The Christian seeks action
p: But the Christian seeks action. We speak against evil, saying truth in love. Not compromising with evil. And not being unequally yoked to wickedness.
p: We love our people. We give relief to them in their poverty, we provide for the widow and give judgment to the fatherless. We share the Gospel that they may do the same, and that our nation can prosper.
refs: Ephesians 4:15; 2 Corinthians 6:14; Isaiah 1:17

--- No Christian should support them
p: But groups that seek violence for its own sake. Who riot in the daytime. Who only know fear and entitled complaining, they are wicked as Hell and you see them led by actual feds, betrayed by CIs, given over to prosecution because they engage in crimes. Immorality and sin. Perversion.
callout: No Christian should support them.

--- A lack of faith
lead: When I hear the fearful and angry calling for insurrection, I see their lack of faith. They don't walk in the spirit and so they fulfill the lusts of the flesh. And they get what they deserve.
p: And of this sin, I am chief. I have and am subject to the same outrage and fears, when I don't walk after the spirit.
refs: Galatians 5:16; 1 Timothy 1:15

--- Offended by Romans 13
p: I have lost friends, who professed Christ and said the things we expect a saved person to confess, who became offended by the idea that they are the cause for our misfortune. That if they had faith they wouldn't be afraid, and not being afraid, able to protect their families and community, blessed by God.
p: They call that weak. They say God doesn't want us to just sit around and let Him do all the work. They claim God expects us to stand up for ourselves.
center: And this is true.

--- What God asks of us
tile: 1 | To read and study His word. [[2 Timothy 2:15]]
tile: 2 | To go to church and work towards edifying it. [[Hebrews 10:25]]
tile: 3 | To preach the Gospel to every creature. [[Mark 16:15]]
tile: 4 | To be instant in prayer. [[Romans 12:12]]
tile: 5 | To help the brokenhearted, to give hope to the hopeless. To win souls. [[Proverbs 11:30]]
p: And, to a man, those that are offended by Romans 13, who are insisting we "do something!" do none of those things.

--- Examine yourselves
p: They may join a church or denomination, seeking an identity. A trad and based label to join, to further their politics. But they don't actually walk as a Christian. They may even recruit others to their denomination, but it's because they are seeking power, not out of compassion to save souls.
lead: Know the signs, examine yourselves. See it in others and make a difference that they turn to God, giving Him His wrath and Vengeance, not taking it themselves.
refs: 2 Corinthians 13:5; Romans 12:19

=== Heal their land
--- God judges nations
lead: But God judges nations based on how the people who call themselves by His name, act.
p: So when we as a nation, White Heritage Americans, Christians, abandoned the faith and our own libertine rights over the blessings of liberty in Christ, the ministers appointed by God, who hold the sword not in vain, turn against us.

--- That's on you. That's on me.
p: Live worthy of a Godly nation, and remember that God's wrath is in His time. But the biggest delay is having a people worth saving because they turned to the Lord. That's on you. That's on me.
lead: It is saved believers turning towards God that saves a nation.

--- A promise of salvation for nations [title]
heading: That's a promise
sub: But God made a promise of salvation for nations too.
big: 2 Chronicles 7:14
take: But so few believe the report....
